Apple's latest software update for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod/">HomePod</a> brings a new Sound Glow feature to the &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj;, &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; mini, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod-mini/">HomePod mini 2</a>. Apple introduced Sound Glow as a &zwnj;HomePod mini 2&zwnj; feature, but it's available for the second-generation &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; and the original &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; mini too.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/homepod-sound-glow.jpg" alt="" width="1915" height="1077" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071677" /><br/>
&zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; Software 27.2 is available as a release candidate update for developers and public beta testers, but it should launch next week. Once you've updated your &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; or &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; mini to the new software, you can go to the &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; settings to turn on Sound Glow. If your HomePods are paired with an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a>, you can also use the &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; Control Center to turn Sound Glow on or off.<br/>
<br/>
With Sound Glow, the top of a &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; or &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; mini lights up with color that pulses in sync with the music or audio that's playing. The feature draws colors from album artwork, and it works with songs, podcasts, Apple's ambient music feature, and more.<br/>
<br/>
Sound Glow is not available on the original &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
